|  One of the earliest critiques of the roles and responsibilities of law
|  guardians appeared in a 1990 treatise on the protective mother problem published by the National Center on Women and Family Law.\3 In
|  Legal Issues and Legal Options in Civil Child Sexual Abuse Cases: Representing the Protective Parent, attorneys H. Joan Pennington and Laurie
|  Woods cautioned that the role of the Guardian Ad Litem, his/her qualifications, rights and duties, and accountability vary from jurisdiction to
|  jurisdiction. Generally, there are no standards, no certification, no requirement of neutrality, and no guarantee that it is the child’s interests
.  being represented (p. 16)

--- Sentence/end 
